{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/collectorencoding\/collectorbatchdecoder"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CollectorBatchDecoder"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let decoder = try CollectorBatchDecoder(plan: try TrackingPlan())","let batch = try decoder.batch(from: body)  \/\/ the body of a POST \/v1\/batches","await destination.receive(batch.records)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record keeps what the body holds of it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":";"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/timestamp"},{"text":", to the millisecond the body holds;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"its event, a value of the decoder’s type of that ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and version, read through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values included;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the context the body’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds: the session’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the sample rate, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard context keys, and the trace context, which the decoder’s instrument extracts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record has no ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/sourceLocation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/deliveryTag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which the body","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t hold, and it reveals its sensitive values, as a tracked record does, so a destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made with ","type":"text"},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" still redacts them. Encoding the records again with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of the same plan, and an instrument that injects what it extracts,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the same bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record is read at the version its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" member states, into the decoder’s type of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that name and version, through the plan’s schema of both. A server that reads the batches of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"several releases of an app is given a type of each version they send. It declares the earlier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"versions in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"private"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fileprivate"},{"type":"text","text":" scope, where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" lets a second type of one name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build, and a plan made from the same types holds a schema of each. That scope is a file-scope"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"private"},{"type":"text","text":" type or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fileprivate"},{"type":"text","text":" one, not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"private"},{"type":"text","text":" member of another type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var items: Int","    var currency: String","}","","\/\/ Version 1, which releases still installed send.","private enum EarlierVersions {","    @Event(name: \"checkout_started\")","    struct CheckoutStarted {","        var items: Int","    }","}","","let decoder = try CollectorBatchDecoder(plan: try TrackingPlan())"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record without a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" member, as releases before the member was written send, is read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at version 1 when the decoder has a type and the plan a schema of its event at 1, and otherwise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the lowest version it has both of. Those releases sent version 1 unless an event declared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another. A record one of them sent at a raised version is read at version 1 too when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decoder has version 1: it is reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError\/undecodableProperty(event:property:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when its properties don’t fit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that type, and read as version 1 when they do."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the decoder can’t read is left out and the batch’s other records are read: one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event it has no type of, one at a version it has no type of or the plan no schema of, a member"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that is missing or holds what the encoder never writes, and a property the event’s type can’t read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder\/batch(from:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns each as an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/UndecodedRecord","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property a delivery redacted is missing, so its record reads back only when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property is optional or has a default value; a redacted "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element of an array is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so a record whose array of non-optional "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" elements was redacted is reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError\/undecodableProperty(event:property:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". An integer outside its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property’s type, such as 300 for a "},{"code":"UInt8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", is reported the same way. A property of a type the plan can’t map reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"back only as far as its JSON holds what its "},{"code":"Decodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance reads: a whole "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside it is written without a fraction, and a "},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside it as a timestamp, neither of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which it reads."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A body that isn’t a collector batch at all throws "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/NotACollectorBatch","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder\/init(plan:events:instrument:)","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder\/init(plan:instrument:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder\/batch(from:)"]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CollectorBatchDecoder"}],"modules":[{"name":"CollectorEncoding"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"CollectorBatchDecoder.sw